WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.026 --> 00:00:20.227
Brody said to Hermes as the crowd murmured in reaction to Zeus' announcement.

2
00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:26.130
"I guess we'll get to check out this Alcides guy for ourselves soon, huh?"

3
00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.570
He glanced around.

4
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.892
"Look, there are Markos and Julia.

5
00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:34.026
Let's see if they bought those eels for dinner.

6
00:00:34.386 --> 00:00:34.947
I'm hungry!"

7
00:00:37.529 --> 00:00:39.110
Hermes didn't seem to hear him.

8
00:00:39.791 --> 00:00:41.232
He was still staring at Zeus.

9
00:00:42.994 --> 00:00:45.115
Meanwhile Ares pushed forward.

10
00:00:45.956 --> 00:00:48.318
Brody gasped when he saw the god of war.

11
00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:52.282
Ares' hair always looked as red as flames.

12
00:00:53.903 --> 00:00:55.985
But now it had turned into real flames!

13
00:00:57.346 --> 00:01:02.490
The people near Ares shrank back, looking nervous as sparks flew from the god's head.

14
00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.973
"We'll be ready for your champion, Zeus!"

15
00:01:06.593 --> 00:01:07.514
Ares called out.

16
00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.955
"I hope he's ready for us."

17
00:01:12.217 --> 00:01:13.058
Zeus smirked.

18
00:01:13.078 --> 00:01:16.280
"Trust me when I say that you won't be ready, Ares.

19
00:01:17.741 --> 00:01:21.824
Nobody in Greece has ever seen anything like Alcides before.

20
00:01:23.105 --> 00:01:27.388
Now excuse me while I go prepare for my champion's arrival."

21
00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.602
"Pay my husband no mind!"

22
00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:35.124
Hera's sharp voice cut through the noise of the crowd.

23
00:01:35.144 --> 00:01:41.529
"I don't know why you're all making such a fuss over his mysterious champion.

24
00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:48.774
Nobody in Olympia has seen Poseidon's champion yet, nor Hades' champion either."

25
00:01:48.794 --> 00:01:52.476
"That's different," Ares snarled.

26
00:01:52.496 --> 00:01:57.600
"Poseidon and Hades aren't telling outrageous tales about their champions."

27
00:01:58.964 --> 00:02:01.505
"Yes," a man in the crowd called out.

28
00:02:01.526 --> 00:02:04.567
"I heard Alcides can read people's minds!"

29
00:02:06.448 --> 00:02:08.749
"Nonsense," Hera spat out.

30
00:02:08.769 --> 00:02:11.011
"No mortal can do that."

31
00:02:12.311 --> 00:02:13.292
Zeus smiled at her.

32
00:02:13.312 --> 00:02:16.354
"We shall see, my dear wife.

33
00:02:17.034 --> 00:02:18.735
Now I really have to go."

34
00:02:19.936 --> 00:02:25.018
Thunder boomed, and lightning sizzled on the dais, so brightly that Brody closed his eyes.

35
00:02:26.779 --> 00:02:29.369
When he opened them again, Zeus was gone.

36
00:02:29.389 --> 00:02:32.871
"Whoa!" Brody said.

37
00:02:32.891 --> 00:02:34.611
"How'd he do that?"

38
00:02:36.092 --> 00:02:42.436
Instead of answering, Hermes grabbed Brody's arm and dragged him over to Apollo, Artemis, and Caerus, who were

39
00:02:42.516 --> 00:02:43.616
all standing nearby.

40
00:02:43.636 --> 00:02:45.857
"What do you think?"

41
00:02:46.318 --> 00:02:47.718
Hermes asked the other gods.

42
00:02:47.738 --> 00:02:51.140
"Will Zeus really show his champion soon?"

43
00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:58.044
Brody didn't pay attention to the other gods' responses because Julia and Markos had just joined the group.

44
00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.781
"Did you see Zeus' lightning trick?"

45
00:03:02.241 --> 00:03:03.122
Brody asked them.

46
00:03:03.142 --> 00:03:04.943
"Totally cool, huh?

47
00:03:05.323 --> 00:03:09.465
And Ares' hair—" Julia cut him off.

48
00:03:10.346 --> 00:03:11.426
"Never mind that, Brody.

49
00:03:11.746 --> 00:03:18.250
We've been talking to some of the other champions, and—" She stopped talking as Hermes suddenly yanked Brody

50
00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:23.253
forward. "And my champion will beat Alcides at every event!"

51
00:03:23.653 --> 00:03:24.913
Hermes bragged loudly.

52
00:03:24.933 --> 00:03:29.396
"He's the best mortal athlete Olympia has ever seen."

53
00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:32.316
"So you keep saying."

54
00:03:33.157 --> 00:03:34.837
Artemis looked Brody up and down.

55
00:03:34.857 --> 00:03:40.138
"I suppose we'll find out soon enough if it's true."

56
00:03:40.159 --> 00:03:47.600
"Being the best athlete won't help your champion if Alcides is as sneaky and ruthless as everyone says,"

57
00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.241
Apollo remarked.

58
00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:58.563
"I heard he killed his music teacher as a boy, and Just then Brody spotted Aphrodite approaching.

59
00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:05.986
"Don't worry, I'll beat Alcides," he said loudly, hoping that the goddess of beauty would hear him.

60
00:04:06.006 --> 00:04:10.968
"I'm going to win every event, like Hermes said—just watch!"

61
00:04:12.969 --> 00:04:17.791
He ran forward and went into a bodybuilder pose right in front of Aphrodite.

62
00:04:17.811 --> 00:04:21.753
"Oh, my," she said with a smile.

63
00:04:21.773 --> 00:04:25.514
"What an impressive display!"

64
00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:29.776
"Thanks." Brody puffed his chest out.

65
00:04:30.552 --> 00:04:31.592
"But this is nothing.

66
00:04:31.953 --> 00:04:33.913
You should see me catch a football!"

67
00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.815
Aphrodite tilted her head, looking confused.

68
00:04:37.835 --> 00:04:40.356
"Catch a football?"

69
00:04:40.876 --> 00:04:41.456
she echoed.

70
00:04:43.597 --> 00:04:45.838
Julia darted over and pulled Brody away.

71
00:04:45.858 --> 00:04:49.520
"Forget about Aphrodite, Brody!"

72
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:50.660
she whispered.

73
00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.981
"We need to talk to Hermes about the chariot thing!"

74
00:04:54.001 --> 00:04:56.402
"What chariot thing?"

75
00:04:56.903 --> 00:05:00.084
Brody asked, but Julia was yanking him toward Hermes.

76
00:05:01.632 --> 00:05:04.173
Brody looked back over his shoulder at Aphrodite.

77
00:05:05.574 --> 00:05:09.215
The beautiful goddess had already turned away to talk to another goddess.

78
00:05:12.337 --> 00:05:15.718
"Excuse me, Hermes," Julia said when they reached the god.

79
00:05:15.738 --> 00:05:18.079
"What is it, girl?"

80
00:05:18.519 --> 00:05:20.700
Hermes asked, sounding distracted.

81
00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.821
"I'm very busy right now."

82
00:05:24.362 --> 00:05:29.964
"I thought you should know that Brody doesn't know anything about horses or chariot driving," Julia said.

83
00:05:31.712 --> 00:05:33.073
"He's never done it before.

84
00:05:33.573 --> 00:05:36.135
Perhaps it would be best to work on that event next?"

85
00:05:36.155 --> 00:05:40.639
"Are you telling me how to train my champion, mortal girl?"

86
00:05:41.239 --> 00:05:42.180
Hermes thundered.

87
00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:43.621
Then he blinked.

88
00:05:43.641 --> 00:05:46.503
"Wait. Perhaps you're right.

89
00:05:46.903 --> 00:05:49.025
I've been meaning to practice for the chariot race."

90
00:05:50.546 --> 00:05:52.247
He patted Julia on the head.

91
00:05:52.267 --> 00:05:54.549
"Thank you for the reminder, mortal.

92
00:05:55.249 --> 00:05:56.930
I'll contact Poseidon right now."

93
00:05:58.171 --> 00:05:58.892
He hurried off.

94
00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.521
Brody whirled toward Julia.

95
00:06:02.541 --> 00:06:04.122
"What was that about?"

96
00:06:04.542 --> 00:06:05.183
he demanded.

97
00:06:05.203 --> 00:06:08.244
"You made me sound like an idiot.

98
00:06:08.464 --> 00:06:09.685
I can drive a chariot!"

99
00:06:09.705 --> 00:06:12.647
"Have you ever driven one before?"

100
00:06:13.147 --> 00:06:13.987
Julia asked.

101
00:06:15.488 --> 00:06:16.229
Brody shrugged.

102
00:06:16.249 --> 00:06:21.812
"No. But I'd never thrown a javelin before, and look how great I am at that!"

103
00:06:23.273 --> 00:06:26.635
Just then Markos emerged from the crowd and hurried over.

104
00:06:26.655 --> 00:06:28.856
"Listen," he said.

105
00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:32.921
"I was just talking to a friend.

106
00:06:33.522 --> 00:06:35.984
His father is a guard at the Temple of Hera.

107
00:06:37.305 --> 00:06:40.227
He says Hera already has a plan to humiliate Zeus."

108
00:06:42.009 --> 00:06:44.891
"That doesn't seem like a big surprise," Julia said.

109
00:06:44.911 --> 00:06:49.094
"I know, but listen," Markos went on.

110
00:06:49.114 --> 00:06:53.918
"Hera doesn't only want to beat Zeus' champion with her own.

111
00:06:54.819 --> 00:06:58.642
She also plans to banish Alcides to Tartarus through some trickery!"

112
00:06:58.662 --> 00:07:01.560
"Tartarus? Really?"

113
00:07:02.101 --> 00:07:02.861
Julia said.

114
00:07:02.881 --> 00:07:06.103
"Tartarus? What's that?"

115
00:07:06.543 --> 00:07:07.304
Brody asked.

116
00:07:07.324 --> 00:07:09.925
"Is it where they make tartar sauce?"

117
00:07:11.126 --> 00:07:15.528
He laughed loudly at his own joke.

118
00:07:16.789 --> 00:07:19.370
Markos looked confused, and Julia frowned.

119
00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:23.473
"This isn't funny, Brody," she snapped at him.

120
00:07:23.493 --> 00:07:26.554
"Tartarus is part of the underworld.

121
00:07:27.015 --> 00:07:28.916
It's the most terrible part, actually."

122
00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.481
She glanced at Markos.

123
00:07:31.501 --> 00:07:34.784
"Can Hera really banish someone there?"

124
00:07:34.804 --> 00:07:38.207
"I don't know," Markos said.

125
00:07:38.227 --> 00:07:40.989
"But one should never underestimate Hera."

126
00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.372
"Right," Julia agreed.

127
00:07:44.392 --> 00:07:47.234
"Brody almost found that out the hard way."

128
00:07:47.254 --> 00:07:48.535
"I did?"

129
00:07:48.975 --> 00:07:49.656
Brody said.

130
00:07:49.676 --> 00:07:52.738
"Yes. You don't remember?

131
00:07:53.679 --> 00:07:56.341
She got Aphrodite to try to poison you with that chiton!

132
00:07:57.823 --> 00:07:59.244
But there's also some good news.

133
00:07:59.784 --> 00:08:04.827
If Hera stays focused on Zeus and Alcides, maybe she won't try to sabotage Brody anymore."

134
00:08:04.847 --> 00:08:08.810
"Maybe." But Markos looked troubled.

135
00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:11.612
"Still, I wouldn't bet my life on it."
